   "text": "This SMILES is my reading of the drawing, built ring by ring. I did not check it with software, and the stereocentres were assigned by hand from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**What the drawing shows**\n- It is a cyanocobalamin-type skeleton in which the cobalt is not bonded to the ring. It is drawn as a separate `Co2+` and a separate cyanide drawn as N\u2261C with a radical dot.\n- The four corrin ring nitrogens are drawn as three imine nitrogens and one NH.\n- The corrin has the following peripheral groups:\n  - Two propionamide-type chains and some of the acetamide side chains are drawn as imidate anions, `C(=N)[O-]`, rather than as primary amides.\n  - One of these chains is a plain propionamide that carries the aminopropanol linker.\n  - The gem-dimethyl carbon is on the top-right ring.\n  - Methyl groups sit on the quaternary carbons, and there are two bridging methyl-bearing carbons.\n- The linker runs from the amide NH through `CH2\u2013CH(CH3)\u2013O\u2013P(=O)(OH)\u2013O` to the ribose 3\u2032-oxygen. The ribose carries a 5-CH2OH, a 2-OH, and a 5,6-dimethylbenzimidazolium on C1\u2032.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each stereocentre from its wedge or hash. These are the ribose carbons, the linker CH(CH3)O carbon, and the corrin carbons carrying side chains or methyls.\n\nSMILES: CC1=C2NC([C@@H](CCC(=N)[O-])[C@]2(C)CC(N)=O)=CC3=NC(=C(C)C4=N[C@@H]([C@@]5(C)[C@@](C)(CC(N)=O)[C@H](CCC(=N)[O-])C1=N5)[C@H](CC(N)=O)[C@@]4(C)CCC(=O)NC[C@@H](C)OP(=O)(O)O[C@@H]6[C@@H](CO)O[C@H]([n+]7c[nH]c8cc(C)c(C)cc78)[C@@H]6O)[C@@H](CCC(=N)[O-])C3(C)C.[Co+2].N#[C]"
